line	<str>You now need to collect the four parts of the key to open the door on Lithkren.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the south-eastern coast of the Kharazi Jungle and down the staircase into the maze. Turn off Auto Retaliate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Navigate to the centre of the maze and take the key piece.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you have taken the Dragon key piece, the plinth can be used to transport you out.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Reldo in the Varrock Castle library.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the second bookcase from the north on the west side of the central row (see this image).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Reldo again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Port Phasmatys and speak to Sarah, west of the bank.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring a dragonstone, 2 molten glass, a glassblowing pipe, and a chisel to Ava in Draynor Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your glassblowing pipe on your dragonstone and use the inert locator orb on Ava to get a locator orb.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to Mort Myre Swamp and use the locator to find the buried key piece. Bring food as the locator hurts you every time you use it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Dig up the dragon key piece.</str>
line	
line	<str>Ask Brundt the Chieftain in Rellekka about the dragonkin fortress. or if you don't own a Seal of Passage or if you haven't started the Fremennik Exiles quest, whichever refers to the fortress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight with Vorkath. See Vorkath/Strategies for recommended setups.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Torfinn on the dock to the north to go to Ungael.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill Vorkath.</str>
line	
line	<str>After you kill him, climb over the ice chunks in the north of the crater (if required you can teleport out to restock for a dungeon part, Vorkath will remain dead).</str>
line	
line	<str>Walk along the path to the north-west of the island and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever in the south-west section, then run to the room on the east wall before the timer runs out (you must have at least 15% run energy).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the stone chest for a dragon key piece and an ancient key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the crypt whose entrance is found in the southern part of the Graveyard of Heroes. Follow the dirt path south to a small building.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the bottom of the crypt and inspect the tomb to find the puzzle.</str>
line	
line	<str>The solution to the puzzle is different for everyone. Refer to the table below to solve this puzzle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the tomb to get the Dragon key piece.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the Ancient Cavern (use a games necklace to teleport to Barbarian Outpost and run south to the whirlpool).</str>
line	
line	<str>Descend the stairs and run south to another set of stairs which lead to the mithril dragon area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Run west and open the mithril door in the middle of the area (with the three mithril dragons clumped together). You need the ancient key to open this door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cast Fire Wave or Fire Surge on the three dragon heads.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the room and go east down the staircase, and then go to the south-western area of the caverns, and climb up the rough hewn steps there.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use one of the anvils here to forge the dragon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Fossil Island and use the Rowboat to Lithkren (west of Mushroom Meadow Mushtree). Return to the area where Dallas Jones is.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Dragon key on the ancient doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the doors and head up north and speak to Dallas to start a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, make sure to finish the dialogue with Jardric and Bob.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Varrock and speak with King Roald about the dragon threat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak with the following rulers "about the dragon threat" in any order:</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Varrock and enter the dining room north of the throne room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make sure to talk to Bob after exiting the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Rellekka and take the boat back to Ungael by speaking to Torfinn.</str>
line	
line	<str>Hold off the assault on your ship for 4 minutes.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>There is a checkpoint after defending the ship from the assault.</col>
step	71	-	Quick guide step 71
line	<str>Talk to Alec Kincade outside the Myths' Guild (spirit tree to Feldip Hills) to start the quest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dallas Jones at the Karamja pub at Musa Point. The fastest way there is amulet of glory to karamja, alternativley to take the boat from Port Sarim.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Elvarg's Lair under Crandor and talk to Dallas Jones (shortcut via the volcano on Karamja).</str>
line	
line	<str>Right-click use your pickaxe on the Northern wall in the room you defeated Elvarg, then enter the tunnel. (Marked on minimap red wall line)</str>
line	
line	<str>Investigate the Ancient Mural to the north. A level 100 spawn will attack you. Kill it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Investigate the mural again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dallas Jones.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to Fossil Island in the basement of the House on the Hill and talk to Dallas Jones.</str>
line	
line	<str>Find the missing 24 map pieces and use them on the map in the middle of the room. Note: You can hand your pieces to Dallas to save inventory space - Hand in 8 map pieces within the house before heading outside to save time.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dallas Jones and solve the map puzzle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dallas Jones again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Jardric at the museum camp.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring 8 oak planks, 10 swamp paste, 12 nails (more may be needed as you may bend them), a hammer, and a saw to the west side of the island (on the coast just south-west of the "Mushroom Meadow" Magic Mushtree) and build a rowboat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dallas Jones and board the boat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west from the boat to the ruined courtyard, and climb up the western stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the trapdoor to the south, down the staircase to the north, and north down another staircase.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dallas Jones.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the skeleton to the east and read Aivas' diary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dallas Jones again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Find Bob the Cat with your Catspeak amulet (e) and talk to him. You may choose to world hop at the Catherby archery shop to find him quickly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Sphinx in Sophanem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring your seal of passage and make sure you have 1 free inventory space! Note: You can still use the bank run by 'Bird's-Eye' Jack without the seal; however, it is needed to speak to the Oneiromancer.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to Lunar Isle and talk to the Oneiromancer.</str>
line	
line	<str>Crush the astral rune with a hammer, then grind the astral rune shards with a pestle and mortar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make a dream potion by filling the dream vial with water (sink west of bank in town) and adding your goutweed and ground astral rune.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a fight, light the Ceremonial Brazier (located in the largest building on the island), and use your Dream potion on the flame.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Bob and Not Bob, then exit out of the dream to gear up if you are not fully prepared. This also allows you to clear out the tinderbox and fill up with combat supplies.</str>
line	
line	<str>Re-enter the dream by talking to Bob outside the brazier, and then head through the barrier and kill Robert the Strong.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Bob again.</str>
line	
line	<str>You now need to collect the four parts of the key to open the door on Lithkren.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the south-eastern coast of the Kharazi Jungle and down the staircase into the maze. Turn off Auto Retaliate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Navigate to the centre of the maze and take the key piece.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you have taken the Dragon key piece, the plinth can be used to transport you out.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Reldo in the Varrock Castle library.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the second bookcase from the north on the west side of the central row (see this image).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Reldo again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Port Phasmatys and speak to Sarah, west of the bank.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring a dragonstone, 2 molten glass, a glassblowing pipe, and a chisel to Ava in Draynor Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your glassblowing pipe on your dragonstone and use the inert locator orb on Ava to get a locator orb.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to Mort Myre Swamp and use the locator to find the buried key piece. Bring food as the locator hurts you every time you use it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Dig up the dragon key piece.</str>
line	
line	<str>Ask Brundt the Chieftain in Rellekka about the dragonkin fortress. or if you don't own a Seal of Passage or if you haven't started the Fremennik Exiles quest, whichever refers to the fortress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight with Vorkath. See Vorkath/Strategies for recommended setups.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Torfinn on the dock to the north to go to Ungael.</str>
line	
